- creates a sqlite db used by dag run during dag tests
airflow db migrate

-- Task Groups - organizes tasks into groups within your dag
- can apply default args to specific group only
- dynamically map over group of tasks
- turn task patterns into module that can be imported into multiple dags
- can be nested
- tasks within a task group are prefixed with the name of the task group, 
    ex. to get the xcom var in a tg: task_ids="check.validate_fields"

-- Trigger Rules - determines the whether to run the task based on the state of upstream tasks
- ALL_SUCCESS - task runs only when all upstream tasks success
- ALL_FAILED - run only when all upstream are failed or upstream failed
- ALL_DONE - run when all upstream are done, regardless if success or failed
- ALL_SKIPPED - only when all upstream are skipped
- ONE_SUCCESS - run when at least 1 upstream success
- ONE_FAILED - run when at least 1 upstream failed
- ONE_DONE - run when at least 1 upstream either success or failed
- NONE_FAILED - if all upstream have either skipped or successfully ran
- NONE_FAILED_MIN_ONE_SUCCESS - all upstream finished, none failed, and at least 1 success
- NONE_SKIPPED - run when no upstream in skipped state
- ALWAYS - run as soon as the dag runs regardless of upstream state

-- TEMPLATES
- help avoid hard coding values, rendered at runtime (when tasks run)
- templates are defined within strings in templateable parameters using {{ }}
- airflow provides variables such as ids, ti, logical_date, etc.
- not all parameters of an Operator are templateable, check template_fields
    in the operator's docs confirm

-- XComs
- to store classes as xcom, you will need to implement a method that
    that serializes that class into a json serielizable object
- size limit: 1gb for postgres, sqlite = 2gb, mysql = 64mb
- to overcome the size limit use s3 as Xcom backend

-- variables
- create a variable using airflow cli
course % astro dev run variables set my_number_2 84

- you could create an env var using .env file but it requires a restart
astro dev restart

- note: can be used to hide vars as this var will not appear 
    in the ui and variables list commands
astro dev run variables list

- get value of variable in cli
astro dev run variables get my_number_2

- variables can be created in tasks using Variable.set()

-- Airflow parameters
- Parallelism: max number of tasks that can run concurrently on each
    scheduler within a single airflow env
- max_active_tasks_per_dag: max number of tasks that can be scheduled
    at the same time across all runs of a dag
    - at the dag level: max_active_tasks
- max_active_runs_per_dag: max number of active dag runs (per dag) that
    the airflow scheduler can create at a time
    - at the dag level: max_active_runs

-- Kubernetes
- The Kubernetes Executor runs each task in an individual Kubernetes Pod
- It sends a message to the KubeAPI that creates a Pod and runs the task in it
- When a task completes, its Pod is terminated and the resources are returned
    to the cluster
- Tasks are isolated from each other
- Task isolation allows granular resource allocation and easier dependency management

- create a namespace named airflow in Kubernetes
kubectl create namespace airflow

- list namespaces available
kubectl get namespaces

- get pods for the airflow namespace
kubectl get pods -n airflow

- forward port 8080 to host 8080
kubectl port-forward svc/airflow-webserver 8080:8080 --namespace airflow

-- Helm - package manager for Kubernetes
- add airflow in Kubernetes
helm repo add apache-airflow https://airflow.apache.org

- update repos
helm repo update

- install airflow application in the airflow namespace
helm install airflow apache-airflow/airflow --namespace airflow --debug

-- backup airflow variables using airflow cli
airflow variables export variables_backup.json

-- backup airflow connections in env format
airflow connections export connections_backup.env --file-format env
